        <!-- Animated GIF, redrawn by the server on every open, so the time is true each
             time the message is looked at rather than true when it was sent. Frame 1 is a
             correct still for Outlook, which never advances past it. -->
        {# IMAGES OFF IS THE COMMON CASE, NOT THE EDGE CASE. Outlook desktop blocks remote
           images by default and so does most corporate mail. The countdown IS the hero, so
           with images off this block has to still carry the deadline:

             · the alt text is STYLED — an unstyled alt renders as 10px browser-default
               serif and reads as a broken attachment rather than as words somebody wrote;
             · width/height are set so a blocked image reserves its box instead of
               collapsing the panel to nothing;
             · the deadline is repeated as real text underneath, which is the line that
               actually does the work when the image never arrives. #}
        <img src="{{ countdown_url }}" width="320" height="104" alt="{{ countdown_alt }}"
